ural deletions in the chimpanzee genome.</article-title><source>PLoS Genet</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>1939</fpage><lpage>1949</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17953488</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000237-Ahnesorg1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahnesorg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>XLF interacts with the XRCC4-DNA ligase IV complex to promote DNA nonhomologous end-joining.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>124</volume><fpage>301</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16439205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000237-Lin1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldman</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Promiscuous patching of broken chromosomes in mammalian cells with extrachromosomal DNA.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>3975</fpage><lpage>3981</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11574679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000237-Lin2"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldman</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Capture of DNA sequences at double-strand breaks in mammalian chromosomes.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>158</volume><fpage>1665</fpage><lpage>1674</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11514454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000237-Moore1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group 